    "media:imagetext": "TAXI, TAKEOFF \u0026 LANDING\nSEATBE\nEMERGENCY EXIT ROW\nSEATING INSTRUCTIONS\nLAND EVACUATION\nEXIT OPER\nAssess outside conditions at Emergency Exits.\nIf fire, water above the door sill or dangerous debris exists,\nDO NOT OPEN! Proceed to another exit.\nB\nSi Ud. está sentado en una fila de asientos cerca de una salida del\navion, y no puede entender, ni hablar,\nni el leer inglés, por favor\nindentifíquese a la tripulación.\nSi vous êtes assis dans une rangée a côté d'une sortie de l'avion, et\nvous ne pouvez pas comprendre, ni parler, ni lire l'anglais,\nS.V.P.\ncontactez l'équipage.\nFalls Sie bei einem Noutausgang sitzen und nicht Englisch verstehen,\nmelden Sie sich bitte bei einem Flugbegleiter.\nAfai oe alala mai i se nofoa o lo'o lata ane i se faitotoa, ae e te le\nmalamalama ile faa-inilisi, fa'amolemole fa'ailoa mai ile auvaa.\nIf you are seated in a designated emergency exit seat:\nU.S. Federal Aviation Regulations require that passengers seated in\nemergency exit seats have sufficient mobility, strength and dexterity\nto open emergency exits in the event that a crewmember is not\navailable to assist.\nPlease notify a crewmember if another seat\nassignment is required if you do not want to, or are unable to help in\nthe event of an emergency for any of the following reasons:\n1. You lack the strength, dexterity or mobility in both arms and\nhands and legs:\nA. To reach upward, sideways and downward to the location of\nthe emergency exit and exit slide operating mechanisms;\nB. To grasp and push, pull, turn or otherwise manipulate those\nmechanisms;\nC. To push, shove, pull or otherwise open emergency exits;\nD. To lift out, hold, deposit on nearby seats or maneuver over\nseatbacks to the next row, objects the size and weight of\noverwing exit doors;\nE. To remove obstructions similar in size and weight of overwing\nexit doors;\nF. To reach the emergency exit expeditiously;\nG. To maintain balance while removing obstructions;\nH.\nTo exit expeditiously;\nTo stabilize an escape slide after deployment; or\nJ. To assist others in getting off the slide and away from the aircraft.\n2. You are less than 15 years of age or lack capacity to perform one\nor more of the above functions without assistance of an adult\ncompanion, parent or other relative.\n3. You cannot understand oral\ncrew instructions related to\nemergency evacuation provided by HAWAIIAN AIRLINES in\nprinted or graphic form or cannot understand oral crew\ncommands in the English language used by the airline.\n4. You cannot see well enough to perform one or more of the above\nfunctions without the assistance of visual aids beyond contact\nlenses or eyeglasses.\n5. You cannot hear well enough to understand instructions shouted\nby crewmembers without assistance beyond a hearing aid.\n6. You cannot impart information verbally to other passengers.\nYou have:\nA.\nA condition or responsibility such as caring for small\nchildren that would prevent you from performing one or\nmore of the above functions, or\nB.\nA condition that might cause you personal harm if you\nperformed one or more of the listed functions.\nNow, prior to takeoff, carefully study and fully understand the functions\nindicated on this Safety Card. Please contact a crewmember if you have\nany questions or require to be reseated.",
